  "title": "Qt: Improve FollowStreamText scroll performance",
  "description": "We turn on mouse tracking in FollowStreamText so that mouse\nmoves without any buttons pressed will cause the hint text\nto update showing to what packet it will jump if clicked.\n\nHowever, we don't want to send the mouse moves with no buttons\npressed to the base QPlainTextEdit class, which causes a large\nnumber of calculations for no reason that slow down scrolling\nespecially in large documents.\n\nIgnore those events, effectively turning off mouse tracking for\nthe base QPlainTextEdit.\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit f1339763f9c8f48be5e4a1bba908d14d6a5fcc78)",
